   "source": [
    "res = llm.invoke(\"what is GENAI?\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "eeadd1c1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "**GENAI** is most commonly used as an abbreviation for **Generative AI**—the branch of artificial intelligence that creates new content (text, images, audio, video, code, etc.) rather than just analyzing or classifying existing data.  \n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## 1. Generative AI (GENAI)\n",
      "\n",
      "| Feature | Description | Typical Tools/Models |\n",
      "|---------|-------------|---------------------|\n",
      "| **What it does** | Produces novel data that resembles a training set. | GPT‑4, Claude, Stable Diffusion, Midjourney, DALL‑E, Jukebox, etc. |\n",
      "| **Core technology** | Large‑scale neural networks (transformers, diffusion models, GANs) trained on massive corpora. | |\n",
      "| **Typical use cases** | • Writing assistants (chatbots, content creation)<br>• Image/video generation (art, design, advertising)<br>• Music & audio synthesis<br>• Code generation & refactoring<br>• Data augmentation for ML training | |\n",
      "| **Benefits** | Rapid prototyping, creative support, personalization, scalability. | |\n",
      "| **Risks & challenges** | • Misuse (deepfakes, disinformation)<br>• Copyright & ownership issues<br>• Bias & fairness in generated content<br>• Resource intensity (compute, carbon footprint) | |\n",
      "| **Regulatory landscape** | Varies by country; e.g., EU’s AI Act, U.S. FTC guidance, Canada’s AI Act. | |\n",
      "\n",
      "### How it works (high‑level)\n",
      "\n",
      "1. **Data collection** – huge datasets (text corpora, image libraries, etc.) are gathered.  \n",
      "2. **Pre‑training** – a transformer or diffusion model learns statistical patterns.  \n",
      "3. **Fine‑tuning** – the base model is adapted to a specific task or style.  \n",
      "4. **Inference** – the model generates new content based on prompts or seed data.  \n",
      "\n",
      "### Example prompt → output\n",
      "\n",
      "- *Prompt*: “Write a short sci‑fi poem about a city that never sleeps.”  \n",
      "- *Output*: A creative poem in the requested style.\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## 2. General AI (sometimes shortened to GENAI)\n",
      "\n",
      "| Feature | Description |\n",
      "|---------|-------------|\n",
      "| **What it is** | An AI system that possesses general intelligence—capable of understanding, learning, and applying knowledge across a wide range of tasks, similar to a human. |\n",
      "| **Current state** | No fully realized General AI exists; research is ongoing in fields like symbolic reasoning, meta‑learning, and neuromorphic computing. |\n",
      "| **Goal** | Achieve *Artificial General Intelligence* (AGI) that can adapt to new situations without task‑specific retraining. |\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "### Quick Take‑aways\n",
      "\n",
      "- **Most people mean “Generative AI”** when they say GENAI.  \n",
      "- It refers to systems that *create* content.  \n",
      "- **General AI** is a more theoretical, future‑oriented concept and is not yet realized.\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "### Want to dive deeper?\n",
      "\n",
      "- **Technical deep dive**: architecture of transformer models, diffusion processes, training pipelines.  \n",
      "- **Ethics & policy**: responsible AI guidelines, copyright issues, AI governance.  \n",
      "- **Practical use**: how to integrate GenAI into your product, cost models, API options (OpenAI, Anthropic, Stability AI, etc.).  \n",
      "\n",
      "Let me know which angle interests you, or if you had a different “GENAI” in mind!\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(res.content)"
   ]
  }
